# A CANDIDATE: OUR LLAMA.CPP ON UPSTREAM'S LATEST (the operator, 2026-11-27: "1.B always" -
# every new engine starts from upstream llama.cpp's master of the day, all our patches on it).
# engine-guard.series line for line, then:
#   0037  llama.cpp at master 8e23278c (2026-11-27; 299 commits after our 78e0529): nine
#         inner patches rebased (0008 0012 0013 0015 0016 0017 0022 0023 0026, the rest
#         apply as they are, none with fuzz), the OmniVoice backbone without the
#         per-tensor scale arguments upstream folded into the tensors (#28898), 0026
#         without its own pooler hunk (upstream's #33122 keeps it; the GELU key also for
#         upstream's BertForSequenceClassification), and LocalAI's own grpc-server
#         fix for the decision API's audio flag (#32578, LocalAI a1937e98).
#         Upstream comes with it, among others: q6_K dequantized in f32 on SYCL
#         (#32726: the bytes of every Q6_K/Q4_K_M model move), BMG decode at D=256 on
#         the FA vector kernel (#30606), the MoE cache's experts selected on another
#         backend (#33133).
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-upstream.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE ON ANOTHER LLAMA.CPP: a build and EVERY gate again - each encoder's run
# validated anew (#32726 moves quantized bytes), the chat, MADLAD, speech, MedCPT,
# parking, the op refusal (docs/notes/llama-cpp-upstream.md).
